<title>USA: U.S. rice weekly export sales highlights - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. rice weekly export sales highlights - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. rice major sales activity in the week ended Aug 29 reported by exporters for the following purchasing countries, in tonnes:</p>
<p>Net Sales:	1996/97		 1997/98</p>
<p> Syria	    10,500		   Nil</p>
<p> Peru	     10,000</p>
<p> Netherlands     6,200-A</p>
<p> Honduras	  3,100-B</p>
<p> Mexico	    2,400-C</p>
<p>A- includes 1,700 tonnes of rough rice switched from Spain. B- includes 2,200 tonnes of rough rice. C- includes 2,100 tonnes of rough rice.</p>
<p>Net sales of 37,000 tonnes were 26 percent below the prior week.</p>
<p>Weekly exports of 66,800 tonnes were 81 percent above a week earlier and more than double the four-week average.</p>
<p>Primary Export Destinations: Jordan, South Africa, Syria, the Philippines, the Netherlands and Honduras.</p>
</text>
